      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Implement the five-checkpoint synthetic draft lab in a separate learner iOS app, then produce a behavior log and ownership note. The existing client remains a read-only reference.",
        "steps": [
          "Write acceptance criteria before reading the worked solution and choose an iOS 17+ learning target.",
          "Create one observable draft with demo displayName, optional reason, derived canReview, and explicit reset().",
          "Build root editing, a modal reason picker with Cancel, and a pushed Review screen using the same model.",
          "Reuse the UIKitMessage and DemoLoadingScreen examples from sessions 010 and 011, with synthetic input and explicit row sizing.",
          "Add model tests for whitespace, absent selection, valid draft, and Reset; manually exercise modal cancellation and returning from Review.",
          "Record the fixture sequence, any actual tests run, and the ownership/persistence note. Do not claim unrun checks passed."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "A whitespace-only name cannot open Review.",
          "Selection updates the shared draft; Cancel preserves an existing choice.",
          "Returning from Review preserves the root draft.",
          "Reset clears name and reason without implicitly replacing navigation.",
          "The UIKit bridge updates its existing controller from current input.",
          "Review's asynchronous work has a view-associated lifetime and a synthetic failure fixture.",
          "The verification note distinguishes executed checks from planned checks."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>Use the following as a worked reference after implementing your version. These types belong in one scratch iOS 17+ module; include the previously explained UIKitMessage, DemoLoader, DemoLoadingModel, and DemoLoadingScreen declarations from sessions 010–011. Foundation supplies trimming, Observation supplies the macro, and SwiftUI supplies the controls.\u003c/p>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-swift\">import Foundation\nimport Observation\nimport SwiftUI\n\nenum PracticeReason: String, CaseIterable, Identifiable {\n    case chat = \"Demo chat\"\n    case checkIn = \"Demo check-in\"\n    var id: Self { self }\n}\n\n@MainActor\n@Observable\nfinal class PracticeDraft {\n    var displayName = \"\"\n    var selectedReason: PracticeReason?\n\n    var canReview: Bool {\n        !displayName.trimmingCharacters(in: .whitespacesAndNewlines).isEmpty\n            &amp;&amp; selectedReason != nil\n    }\n\n    func reset() {\n        displayName = \"\"\n        selectedReason = nil\n    }\n}\n\n@MainActor\nstruct PracticeRoot: View {\n    @State private var draft = PracticeDraft()\n    @State private var showsPicker = false\n\n    var body: some View {\n        NavigationStack {\n            Form {\n                Section(\"Synthetic input\") {\n                    TextField(\"Demo display name\", text: $draft.displayName)\n                    Button(draft.selectedReason?.rawValue ?? \"Choose demo reason\") {\n                        showsPicker = true\n                    }\n                }\n                Section {\n                    NavigationLink(\"Review\") {\n                        PracticeReview(draft: draft)\n                    }\n                    .disabled(!draft.canReview)\n                    Button(\"Reset\") { draft.reset() }\n                }\n            }\n            .navigationTitle(\"Practice draft\")\n            .sheet(isPresented: $showsPicker) {\n                PracticePicker(draft: draft)\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n@MainActor\nstruct PracticePicker: View {\n    @Environment(\\.dismiss) private var dismiss\n    let draft: PracticeDraft\n\n    var body: some View {\n        NavigationStack {\n            List(PracticeReason.allCases) { reason in\n                Button(reason.rawValue) {\n                    draft.selectedReason = reason\n                    dismiss()\n                }\n            }\n            .navigationTitle(\"Demo reason\")\n            .toolbar {\n                Button(\"Cancel\") { dismiss() }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n@MainActor\nstruct PracticeReview: View {\n    let draft: PracticeDraft\n    var body: some View {\n        Form {\n            Text(draft.selectedReason?.rawValue ?? \"No selection\")\n            UIKitMessage(message: \"Demo name: \\(draft.displayName)\")\n                .frame(height: 100)\n            DemoLoadingScreen(id: draft.selectedReason?.rawValue ?? \"demo-1\")\n        }\n        .navigationTitle(\"Review\")\n    }\n}\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003cp>The Boolean conjunction \u003ccode>&amp;&amp;\u003c/code> requires both validity conditions. Root State retains the draft; the picker writes that same object through its plain reference. Bindable is unnecessary here because its buttons assign a property directly rather than requiring a Binding projection. Its Cancel action only dismisses, so an existing choice remains. Review uses ordinary observable reads and a dynamic UIKit message. The modal's separate stack supplies its own toolbar scope. Reset mutates the draft explicitly; it does not use a random ID or replace the stack.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the failure checkpoint, temporarily pass the literal \u003ccode>\"fail\"\u003c/code> to DemoLoadingScreen in your own scratch version, then restore the reason-based input. A model test should assign a whitespace name and a reason and expect false, assign Demo Ada and expect true, call reset and expect empty name, nil reason, and false. The worked code is a reference design inspected for consistency; it is not a claim that an app binary or screenshot was produced.\u003c/p>"
      },
