      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Produce a full profiling investigation for one bounded synthetic change and a regression-gate proposal. Leave any unexecuted measurement explicitly pending.",
        "steps": [
          "Freeze baseline/candidate, fixture revision, primary hypothesis, correctness invariants, and experiment matrix.",
          "Prepare a mapping XCTest harness, signposted user-operation path, repeatable gesture, and memory route cycle in a scratch target.",
          "Run available checks, then collect diagnostic traces and matched minimally instrumented raw samples when device/tools permit.",
          "Compute declared summaries per cohort, retain failures, and explain phase attribution without summing unrelated p95 values.",
          "Write correctness-first gate rules, artifact references, rollback condition, ownership, and unresolved specialist work."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "Each claim is labeled measured, source-derived, theoretical, or pending.",
          "Observed results include raw samples, sample count, estimator, matching environment, and correctness evidence.",
          "No simulator result certifies phone rendering, memory pressure, or energy.",
          "A timeout/unfinished async task cannot silently become a completed latency sample.",
          "Gate policy uses observed variance and user relevance, with a bounded failure/review action.",
          "The lab leaves client source and learner completion state unchanged."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>A worked investigation chooses one candidate: moving an unchanged stable-row projection from repeated view evaluation to the accepted data-revision boundary. It first proves ordering, equality, empty/error state, insertion/reordering identity, and cancellation behavior. The hypothesis is reduced redundant synchronous main-thread work; competing image and render costs remain visible. No candidate timing is supplied by this answer.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The report records a frozen synthetic fixture and separate simulator and physical-device cohorts. Its raw table has revision, cohort, sample index, outcome, preparation, total operation time, projection time, cache state, and thermal notes. Summary fields contain n, median, nearest-rank p95, range, failures, and conditions only after collection. A diagnostic trace identifies selected intervals and attribution; an equivalent minimal-instrumentation batch confirms the primary operation. A memory sheet separates pixel estimates, transient peak, and route-exit retention. An energy sheet stays pending until supported device observations exist.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The gate proposal says: “Reject incorrect or stale output first. For the declared fixture/cohort, compare the candidate with the established usability and hitch budgets and the paired baseline distribution. Preserve raw artifacts. If the result fails or the effect is within unexplained noise, inspect/reproduce under the same protocol; do not automatically relax thresholds. Revert the isolated candidate when its measured regression is established.” Numeric budgets are filled from real baseline data and product requirements, not guessed here.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The handoff lists benchmark target, selected plan/runner, command and tool versions, result bundle, trace, fixture, and preparation procedure. It states whether any code merely type-checked, tests actually ran, or device profiling actually happened. A peer should be able to replay one cohort without asking what “warm” meant. If hardware is unavailable, the completed artifact is a validated design with pending device evidence, not a fabricated performance improvement. The learner still performs and records the experiment.\u003c/p>"
      },
