      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Build a synthetic web-boundary design with an origin predicate, narrow bridge contract, cookie-readiness gate, and authentication-attempt ledger. Do not open a real identity provider.",
        "steps": [
          "Run URL predicate fixtures for trusted HTTPS, deceptive host, HTTP, credentials, and unexpected port.",
          "Specify which messages and frames CourseBridge accepts; test its validation through an extracted pure decision seam.",
          "Gate fake cookie setup, invalidate account ownership, then release setup.",
          "Define document and authentication generations and reject late callbacks.",
          "Write pending WebKit/device/controlled-provider checks separately from fake results."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "Origin matching uses parsed properties rather than URL substrings.",
          "Unknown bridge fields, commands, or origins cannot invoke native actions.",
          "Account invalidation blocks a late cookie setup from starting an old page.",
          "Navigation decisions and authentication terminal reporting occur once.",
          "No fake test is presented as live cookie sharing or production authentication verification."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>The worked policy allows only the synthetic HTTPS origin for credential eligibility and a single main-frame close command for the bridge. It distinguishes origin eligibility from route parsing and actual TLS trust. Give each document an incrementing generation, and remove the named handler when that document's native capability ends.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Use this MainActor value to model the readiness decision without a web view or real cookies:\u003c/p>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-swift\">@MainActor\nfinal class WebAttemptGate {\n    private var generation = 0\n\n    func begin() -&gt; Int {\n        generation += 1\n        return generation\n    }\n\n    func invalidate() { generation += 1 }\n\n    func isCurrent(_ ticket: Int) -&gt; Bool {\n        ticket == generation\n    }\n}\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003cp>Capture begin's ticket before cookie work. After awaiting the fake, check cancellation, account/document ownership, and isCurrent before starting a load. No await should separate the final decision from the load call on MainActor. Authentication has a separate attempt owner with terminal state; a valid redirect for attempt one must still fail ownership after attempt two begins.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The fixture matrix accepts a trusted origin and one close body, rejects deceptive host and extra fields, rejects a subframe, and ignores callbacks after invalidation. For retention review, draw owner to web view to configuration/content controller to handler, then identify the weak edge and explicit removal. Add page termination and teardown to the pending platform matrix.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The checkout review states that cookies are awaited before load and initial bearer attachment has login/domain/HTTPS predicates, while native logout deletes selected HTTP cookies. It asks for evidence covering the selected WebKit data store and redirects rather than claiming a leak. No SDK internals or identity-provider runtime flow were verified by this worked answer.\u003c/p>"
      },
