      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Build the synthetic surface-command actor and an integration evidence ledger. Review actual widget, intent, and App Group sources without changing client code or learner progress.",
        "steps": [
          "Apply one command twice and assert applied then duplicate with one visible acknowledgment.",
          "Reset ownership before releasing a delayed command and assert stale with no recreated data.",
          "Add unknown-card and failed-durable-write rows to the design.",
          "Trace manifest embedding, shared store location, timeline placeholders, and intent routing.",
          "Create a ledger for explained behavior, executed fakes, pending target/device/distribution checks, and the listed specialist branches."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "Repeated commands cannot duplicate the synthetic effect.",
          "Old ownership cannot resurrect cleared records.",
          "The actor is labeled memory-only and single-process.",
          "Widget reload is not described as an exact scheduling or instant privacy guarantee.",
          "Repository support is distinguished from unimplemented specialist platforms.",
          "The final ledger includes all seven sessions with measurable boundary outcomes."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>The worked test starts with the actor's current epoch and builds a SurfaceCommand for card alpha with a synthetic operation ID. The first apply returns applied; the second returns duplicate; values contains alpha once. Start another command, hold its release in a fake, resetOwner, and then apply it. The result is stale and the acknowledged Set remains empty. Apply a current-epoch unknown card to verify unknownCard without mutation.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The integration ledger makes ownership and evidence reviewable:\u003c/p>\u003ctable>\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Boundary\u003c/th>\u003cth>Acceptance\u003c/th>\u003cth>Evidence still needed\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>Background/notification\u003c/td>\u003ctd>One completion; expired or old-account work cannot commit\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Signed-device APNs and execution observations\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>Route/login\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Bounded parser; only current pending route navigates\u003c/td>\u003ctd>AASA, installed identity, cold/warm taps, App Clip invocation\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>Foundation/storage\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Named civil-time policy; correct ranges; preserved failures\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Locked-file attributes, upgrade fixtures, backup behavior\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>Web/device services\u003c/td>\u003ctd>No stale cookie, document, permission, or selection commit\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Controlled provider, WebKit, hardware and Settings behavior\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>Widget/intent\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Stable command identity; no stale record resurrection\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Interprocess transaction, signed App Group, cached snapshot review\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003cp>A durable command design records operation identity and effect atomically under current account ownership. The process that renders a timeline reads an immutable projection, not an app-owned managed object. If the write fails, define a bounded visible failure outcome and do not report durable success merely because perform returned a result. Request reload after successful state changes and cleanup, while acknowledging system-controlled rendering.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The source review records active MedicationWidget embedding, the placeholder/snapshot distinction, the group path helper and its fallback, BookAgain's app-opening route, and MarkDoseTaken's shared mutation path. It calls out read-modify-write coordination and suppressed write errors as questions needing verification, not reproduced incidents. The specialist ledger names media/DSP, Metal, Bluetooth, HealthKit/regulatory, StoreKit, watchOS/visionOS, CloudKit, ML, specialized extensions, and unsafe APIs as further study.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Run only the synthetic actor and parser/service fakes in your scratch work. No signed extension, real widget refresh, production account, or course progress is changed by this worked answer. Your submission adds actual results to the ledger and leaves unexecuted checks clearly pending.\u003c/p>"
      },
