        "solution": "\u003cp>Settings uses SplitBrowser directly, with tabItem and LibraryTab.settings attached to that root. The split view manages column navigation, while BrowseStack owns a separate typed push path. For an unavailable fixture, construct RouteDetail with a valid but unknown synthetic UUID and the existing notes. It should display its recovery message without force-unwrapping a failed record lookup.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A correct route sequence is empty path → one note route → empty path after Back or removeAll. Selecting a tab changes LibraryTab, not that route's record identifier. The split sequence starts with nil, becomes a chosen UUID and resolves its current record. Restoration should validate any stored route against current records and user scope, discarding or recovering invalid destinations. That policy is additional work beyond this in-memory example. Record the actual compact and expanded interactions, including toolbars and return behavior, rather than declaring adaptive navigation passed from one phone screenshot.\u003c/p>"
