        "solution": "\u003cp>The supplied pass arrays yield baseline median 109.5 and p95 118, candidate median 99.5 and p95 108. Regression yields candidate median 129.5 and p95 138, violating 130 and the allowed 10-percent increase. Invalid preparation reports a candidate preparation-failure rate of one with no valid measured attempt. Missing data rejects the claimed completion without a duration. These are predicted fixture results until the learner executes the commands, and actual script outputs should agree.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the additional schedule, append two distinct measurement records with prepared true, timeout outcome, and null milliseconds. The twenty completed candidate samples still yield p95 108, but twenty-two attempts now include two timeouts. The rate is about 9.09 percent, exceeding the synthetic absolute 5-percent limit and the allowed 2-percentage-point increase. The test suite exercises this mutation. A reviewer preserves those failed outcomes, diagnoses under a bounded protocol, and collects appropriate device evidence before making a product decision.\u003c/p>"
