        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>For conformance, compare the protocol requirement and implementation: operation name, argument labels, parameter and return types, and throwing or asynchronous effects. For an unavailable module, inspect the consuming target, exposed product, import name, dependency edge, and platform. For compiling but unexecuted tests, inspect target inclusion, framework discovery, and the scheme's test action, then look for an actual run artifact.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The installed compiler alone cannot settle any of those questions. Its version differs from manifest tools requirements, effective language mode, SDK, and deployment target. Write the selected build route beside each finding. In the walkthrough, keep source-visible facts separate from predicted consequences and checks you have executed. A verified source glob supports membership; a test result supports execution; an isolated program supports only its own language and ownership behavior. A useful handoff names the narrow next check and its expected evidence rather than promising that regeneration will fix every category.\u003c/p>",
