        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>The initializer supplies an initial value when storage is created for an identity. A changed parent input does not necessarily overwrite existing State for the same identity. That behavior can preserve unsaved edits, but here it can also leave record A's draft visible while the parent expects B. Inspect identity and model ownership before assuming observation failed.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Choose an explicit contract: have the parent own the active draft, implement a replace-record operation with unsaved-edit handling, or use a stable record-based identity when a record switch should create a fresh editor. A random UUID on every render repeatedly destroys local state and explains the erased typing. Test that an unrelated parent change preserves edits, that switching records follows the chosen confirmation or reset rule, and that explicit Reset behaves independently. Keep model initialization free of required side effects because description construction can create candidate instances without replacing existing storage. Persistence remains a separate requirement.\u003c/p>",
