        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Assign distribution containment to the release owner and launch diagnosis to the client owner using matching symbols. Pause further rollout progression where supported, while acknowledging that this does not downgrade installed build 410 or eliminate all new installations. The launch trap needs a newly versioned, built, signed, tested, and submitted corrective release because configuration cannot protect a path that crashes before it is read.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the separate UI defect, compare compatible flag disablement with a binary fix and state offline or cached-configuration delays. Assign the service owner to restoring a response contract compatible with older installed clients; data changes may need forward repair. Retain the new archive, symbols, configuration, clean-install and upgrade evidence. Define resumption using confirmed task completion and diagnostics for affected cohorts, with enough volume and reporting-delay allowance. A beta upload, green CI, or release pause alone is not recovery. The runbook describes these branches and their owners without pretending that the synthetic build was distributed or repaired.\u003c/p>",
