        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Relabel the device plan and release tabletop as planned work. A source cleanup review supports an observation about the traced code, not a reproduced leak or deployed repair. Executed mapper fixtures can support the specific input-output contract under their test conditions, but do not establish faster user interaction. A checklist's existence likewise does not prove another team adopted it or avoided failures.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For every claim, attach the method, fixture, environment, artifact, contribution, and limitation. Production performance needs the defined user boundary and representative measurements; reliability needs build, cohort, denominator, reporting coverage, and window. Reproduction needs enough setup for another engineer to investigate, yet may still leave production causality unresolved. Cross-reference the feature trace, tests, threat model, incident note, and release ledger so inconsistent assumptions surface. Use those gaps to select the next bounded responsibility and review. Neither a complete course nor a polished portfolio guarantees exhaustive iOS competence or a staff title.\u003c/p>",
