        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Prefer a small owned feature with targeted platform review when the evidence gaps are device diagnosis and artifact validation. Compare a shared concurrency migration's broader semantic risk and a guideline's limited value without adoption evidence. Name the feature owner and specialist reviewers, then set two concrete tasks: reproduce a lifecycle cancellation case with diagnostics and validate an archive, matching symbols, and installation path.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Gate delivery on behavior, accessibility, privacy, and release artifacts; use comparable task-outcome measures after deployment. Expand scope when independent execution and review evidence support it, rather than from a framework count. For the tabletop pre-configuration failure, assign distribution containment and a corrective binary, while preserving service compatibility for older clients; flags cannot repair that launch path. Measure team influence through reviewed adoption or reduced recurring cost, not the guideline's existence. Record planned versus observed artifacts, residual review needs, and when to reassess. This handoff owns decisions and recovery without pretending that learning exercises already produced customer outcomes.\u003c/p>",
