        "lesson": "029",
        "level": "Foundation",
        "kind": "Explain",
        "prompt": "Explain which view grows and which shrinks in a title-and-badge row. How do hugging and compression priorities express different decisions?",
        "scenario": "A synthetic row needs a 180-point title, a 60-point badge, and 12 points of spacing. Its parent supplies either 300 or 220 points.",
        "minutes": 5,
        "androidBridge": "ConstraintLayout and Compose measurement help frame size negotiation, but Swift intrinsic-size priorities are optional inequalities, not Kotlin layout weights or Compose hard constraints. Raising hugging does not raise compression resistance.",
