        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A diffable snapshot describes section and item identity plus order. An unchanged identifier does not necessarily cause UIKit to configure its cell again when an external content dictionary changes. Keep A as an immutable identifier, update its content in the lookup, and explicitly mark surviving changed IDs for reconfiguration. A newly inserted C receives initial configuration; it is not a surviving item. Identifiers must be unique across the snapshot.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Do not synthesize identity from the entire mutable display model: changing a subtitle could then look like replacing the item. Reconfiguration preserves an existing cell and does not call prepareForReuse for that update, so configuration must set every relevant visual and accessibility property. Reserve reload behavior for changes such as needing a different cell kind. Apply the content revision and snapshot through a serialized UI owner. Selection should resolve or capture A's domain ID rather than offset zero, which becomes C after insertion. Test subtitle changes, reorder, duplicate IDs, and delayed image completion separately.\u003c/p>",
