        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Padding followed by background attaches decoration outside the padded result, so the added margins are colored. Background followed by padding colors the original text extent and adds uncolored space afterward. Each modifier returns another description around the preceding one; it does not mutate one Android View in place. Frame, padding and offset therefore have different layout effects.\u003c/p>\u003cp>InfoCard's Content parameter is constrained to View. Its @ViewBuilder initializer lets callers supply multiple or conditional view expressions that become typed content. The initializer evaluates that closure and stores the resulting description. Some View hides a concrete return type without becoming an unrestricted box. No request should start from this content closure or body. A strong answer also chooses HStack, VStack or ZStack according to child relationships rather than merely reproducing a screenshot.\u003c/p>",
