        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A1 and A2 share the same query text, so text equality cannot identify the current request. Assign a new token for each requested generation and invalidate it synchronously when the query changes. Capture the expected token before awaiting and require that token to remain current before publishing. Guard failure as well as success; an obsolete error can otherwise hide newer valid results.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Task cancellation complements this check but cannot replace it. Build a fixture that signals request start and lets the test release outcomes despite cancellation. Start A1, then B, then A2, finish A2 first and await its commit, then release old success and old error and assert the current output remains. Also invalidate without a new request and verify the old outcome is rejected. Use completion gates, not guessed sleeps, and report producer cancellation separately from UI freshness.\u003c/p>",
