        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>The visible row may be a tracked pending insertion or edit. Query output does not prove save succeeded. Catch the save error and report the pending state honestly. Define retry or discard behavior: retry attempts the context's pending changes again, while rollback discards all pending changes in that context. Do not present it as a harmless per-row undo when another editor has unsaved changes.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Container setup failure is a separate boundary from a failed later save. Display a bounded recovery state and gather diagnostics without automatically deleting persisted data. A fresh-context fetch after a successful save is useful local evidence, and a disk-backed relaunch checks durability separately. An in-memory preview cannot establish that restart claim. Migration, uniqueness, cloud and account policies require additional scoped design rather than a destructive reset to make the sample appear healthy.\u003c/p>",
