        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A dependency waits for the prerequisite's finished state. Finished includes cancellation and failed work, so the presenter may become ready with no report. Define a protected optional Result or a domain terminal enum: success carries a value, failure carries the supported recovery, and a stopped prerequisite cannot masquerade as a successful empty report. The graph orders state availability; the consumer owns interpretation.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Check that the builder's BlockOperation performs finite synchronous work. If it starts a callback request and immediately returns, the operation finishes too early; either use the existing async API directly or implement a correctly reviewed asynchronous Operation state machine. Keep dependencies acyclic and add them before enqueueing.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The feature owner should cancel obsolete operations, suppress stale publication and release retained work. A concurrency limit of two does not bound queued payloads, so add admission limits. Test success, failure and cancellation-before-start with reversed enqueue order and controlled completion. Recover by withholding invalid publication and preserving the prior report if product policy allows, then verify cleanup before rolling the repair beyond the scratch fixture.\u003c/p>",
