        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Begin with ownership: keep one vertical scroll owner and make the horizontal strip orthogonal unless independently scrolling vertical content is essential. Leave native arbitration intact before adding custom gestures. A broad zero-distance or high-priority drag can steal page scrolling and still fail after cancellation. If same-axis nesting is necessary, specify its viewport, handoff, and accessible alternatives rather than translating Compose nestedScroll callbacks literally.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Use a single optional Field enum for editing focus, with a unique case on each TextField. On submit, advance to the intended field and request scrolling through the current ScrollViewReader proxy and stable field ID. Validation can clear editing focus and separately request assistive focus on an installed error element. That does not guarantee a software keyboard, announcement, or hardware Tab order.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Compare a simpler stacked form with the custom container if overflow remains unclear. Assign a feature owner for focus/validation and a container owner for layout/arbitration. Verify diagonal drags, software submit/toolbar progression, Tab and Shift-Tab, VoiceOver reading/activation, large text, and RTL on named destinations. Keep drafts intact during cancellation. Compiler and host geometry checks are useful but do not certify those runtime outcomes.\u003c/p>",
