        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Use one strict parser for initial and later URL/activity delivery, then a scene-owned routing reducer. A valid incoming Beta should outrank stale restored Alpha. Define invalid-input behavior explicitly: this lab's cold model falls back to root, while invalid warm input preserves the current route. Restore only recognized schema and IDs, and validate the current account, authorization, and record existence before revealing protected content.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Store small presentation values in SceneStorage, but protect drafts with durable transactions and recovery. Capture an account epoch around async validation so a prior account cannot commit navigation after logout. A view's later onAppear must not overwrite an already accepted external intent with stale restoration.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Request finite background execution before protected work, handle an invalid identifier, and capture an attempt generation in expiration and completion. Retirement clears acceptance, cancels work, makes the identifier invalid, and ends the old identifier once. Old callbacks must not end a replacement. The documented five-second callback budget is not a fixed grant for arbitrary async work.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Assign routing and storage owners, compare immediate checkpoints with a separately scheduled durable job where appropriate, and define recovery after interrupted writes. Host tests establish parser/precedence logic; installed cold/warm delivery, actual expiration, two-window behavior, and durability require independent evidence.\u003c/p>",
