        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Purchase success includes a verification result; the application must inspect that result before granting a right. Finishing means the transaction no longer needs delivery processing, so the recoverable fulfillment effect should exist before finish. Current entitlement is a product-specific projection of verified evidence, not a permanent Boolean copied from the purchase screen. A refund can change facts relevant to the same transaction identity, so a seen-ID filter must not discard all subsequent revocation evidence.\n\nFor the permanent theme, reconcile known verified, non-revoked transactions and listen for updates under a long-lived owner. Offline signed evidence can authenticate a known purchase while failing to reveal a refund that happened remotely after disconnection. Define that freshness policy and explain it to support. A consumable requires an independently durable credit ledger; a subscription needs status and expiration/grace policy. Android acknowledgment experience helps with replay discipline, but is not an exact substitute for StoreKit's verification, finish and entitlement contracts. The synthetic model injects verification and proves none of the actual signature or sandbox behavior.\u003c/p>",
