        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A defensible choice could be a watch Mark packed action for a frequent wrist-friendly task. Compare it with the existing phone checklist, then define latest snapshot context separately from queued commands. The authoritative store applies operation identity and account generation atomically with a receipt; watch UI owns pending state and recovery after a lost reply. Unsupported or opted-out users retain the phone task.\n\nName the phone/watch protocol owner and the support owner, and require paired-device delivery/failure observations before promoting adoption. A simulator can check layout but not transport budgets. If choosing visionOS instead, begin with a window and system controls, which support indirect selection without exposing raw gaze; hardware comfort is separate evidence. Bluetooth needs protocol/device validation, and HealthKit needs type-scoped purpose plus ambiguous-read UX. Stage the feature behind a product decision and define a reversal condition such as unresolved pending-action confusion or unacceptable support burden. No assumed benefit, course attendance or host success establishes user adoption or a full platform integration.\u003c/p>",
